  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This ribbed and cabled beanie is worked bottom-up in the round with an 8-stitch repeat alternating 2 x 2 rib and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "c4f"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "C4F"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " cables, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction keeps the rib and cable columns continuous from cast-on to crown. The rib panels provide elasticity while the cables add texture and visual interest. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the full circumference on one needle. About 100 g (180 m) of worsted yarn. The combined pattern compresses about 5% more than plain rib."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Worsted-weight wool yarn",
              "qty": "100 g (approx. 180 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 7 / US 7)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Cable needle",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "19 sts x 26 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in rib-and-cable pattern on 4.5 mm needles, blocked. The rib panels compress the width; always swatch the combined pattern. At 20 sts per 10 cm the crown closes at 52 cm for size S -- work size M instead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k -- knit; p -- purl"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "C4F -- cable 4 front: sl 2 to cable needle front, k2, k2 from cable needle"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k2tog -- knit two together, right-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 4 mm needle, cast on 96 (100, 104) sts (must be multiple of 8). Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on 4 mm: (4 x 104) / 10 + 15 = 57 cm; round up to 62 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 12 rounds of *k2, p2; repeat from * to end. Switch to 4.5 mm needle. After the brim, you should have 96 (100, 104) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern round: *k2, p2, k4; repeat from * to end. Work 3 plain rounds, then 1 cable round: *k2, p2, C4F; repeat from * to end. Continue until hat measures 20 cm from cast-on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transition round: knit all. Place 8 markers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 88 (92, 96) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating until 32 sts, then every round until 12 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 12 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 12 sts, pull firmly, fasten on inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rib columns not aligning with cable columns: the cast-on count was not a multiple of 8. Rip back and recount."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hat finished 3 cm too small: rib-and-cable pattern compresses more than stocking stitch. Always swatch in pattern and block before measuring."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cable crosses not crisp: tension on the yarn after returning the cable needle stitches is too loose. Pull firmly on the first stitch after the cable cross."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Block over a bowl; wet-blocking sets the cable definition."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool, squeeze without wringing, reshape and dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The double cable hat adds a second cable column in each panel for a denser, more textured result."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}